Upstream projects
-----------------
- GitLab sast-rules (https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/security-products/sast-rules): MIT (rules marked MIT), Apache-2.0 (rules derived from gosec and bandit); Copyright (c) 2011-present GitLab Inc.
- 0xdea semgrep-rules (https://github.com/0xdea/semgrep-rules): MIT; Copyright (c) 2022 raptor
- elttam semgrep-rules (https://github.com/elttam/semgrep-rules): MIT; Copyright (c) 2020 Semgrep (as stated in the upstream LICENSE)

Test fixtures (files next to a rule, used only by opengrep --test) keep
their upstream licence line. Fixtures marked LGPL-3.0 (from find-sec-bugs
and security-code-scan, via GitLab sast-rules) are licensed under
LGPL-3.0 (LICENSES/LGPL-3.0-only.txt, LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt). Release
bundles contain rule files only, never fixtures.

